From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NSY G68-Plus port
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: support regulator-init-microvolt

Mainline gained DT support for specifying an initial voltage only in
6.15; 6.12 parses neither the property nor applies an initial voltage,
and the microvolts sysfs attribute is read-only, so there is no way to
move a rail away from whatever duty the bootloader left programmed.

The NSY G68-Plus has no PMIC: vdd_cpu/vdd_npu/vdd_logic/vdd_gpu are
PWM-controlled bucks and the stock firmware sets them up via
regulator-init-microvolt (e.g. vdd_npu 0.9 V). Port the support back to
6.12 so the DT property works as intended:

  - of_regulator.c: parse "regulator-init-microvolt" into constraints->init_uV
  - machine.h: carry the new field
  - core.c: apply it in set_machine_constraints() before first enable

--- a/drivers/regulator/core.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/core.c
@@ -1436,6 +1436,18 @@
 	ret = machine_constraints_voltage(rdev, rdev->constraints);
 	if (ret != 0)
 		return ret;
+
+	if (rdev->constraints->init_uV > 0) {
+		ret = regulator_set_voltage_rdev(rdev,
+						 rdev->constraints->init_uV,
+						 rdev->constraints->init_uV,
+						 PM_SUSPEND_ON);
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			rdev_err(rdev, "failed to apply init voltage: %pe\n",
+				 ERR_PTR(ret));
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
 
 	ret = machine_constraints_current(rdev, rdev->constraints);
 	if (ret != 0)
--- a/drivers/regulator/of_regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/of_regulator.c
@@ -190,6 +190,9 @@
 				(pval) ? REGULATOR_ACTIVE_DISCHARGE_ENABLE :
 					REGULATOR_ACTIVE_DISCHARGE_DISABLE;
 	}
+
+	if (!of_property_read_u32(np, "regulator-init-microvolt", &pval))
+		constraints->init_uV = pval;
 
 	if (!of_property_read_u32(np, "regulator-initial-mode", &pval)) {
 		if (desc && desc->of_map_mode) {
--- a/include/linux/regulator/machine.h
+++ b/include/linux/regulator/machine.h
@@ -217,6 +217,7 @@
 
 	unsigned int ramp_delay;
 	unsigned int settling_time;
+	unsigned int init_uV;
 	unsigned int settling_time_up;
 	unsigned int settling_time_down;
 	unsigned int enable_time;
